<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25003" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διακοπή</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>gash, cleft,</i> as in the skull,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>VC</u>
				7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				7.38
			</span></i>; <i>deepseated wound,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				18(1).27
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διακοπαὶ σωμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Mar.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			; <i>severance</i> of a musical string, Theo Sm.<i><span class="en">
				p.71
			</span></i> H. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>rupture</i> of a blood-vessel, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.457
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>cutting</i> or <i>canal</i> through an isthmus or mountain,
				<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				1.3.18
			</span></i> (pl.); through a wall or dam, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1188.8
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>; <i>narrow channel</i> or <i>passage,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Jb.</u>
				28.4
			</span></i>, al., cf. <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				7.4.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>divorce,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sm.
				<u>De.</u>
				24.3(1)
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> metaph.,
				<i>breach, rupture, quarrel,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Jd.</u>
				21.15
			</span></i>: pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. φίλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Vett.Val.
					3.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b>
			<i>refutation,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1.11
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>VI.</b>
			<i>intermission,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Herod.Med.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				6.20.19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>VII.</b> Gramm.,
				<i>tmesis,</i> Charis.<i><span class="en">
				p.275
			</span></i> K.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
